content.content:
{"result":"{
  "id": "19105",
  "key": "SFCC-689",
  "summary": "Regional Storefronts — EU Language Mismatch Modal",
  "customfield_10231": {
    "value": "1. Given a shopper lands on the EU Domestic storefront and their browser-detected language matches one of the four supported EU languages (EN, FR, IT, ES) but does not match the current EU locale URL, when the page loads on their first visit, then the language mismatch prompt is displayed automatically.\n2. Given a shopper lands on the EU Domestic storefront and their browser-detected language either matches the current EU locale URL or does not match any of the four supported EU languages, when the page loads, then the language mismatch prompt is not displayed.\n3. Given the prompt is displayed, when it renders, then it shows the shopper's detected language and the current storefront language with two CTAs: one to switch to their detected language and one to stay in the current language.\n4. Given the shopper clicks the switch CTA, when confirmed, then the storefront redirects to the EU locale URL matching their detected language (e.g. /fr-eu/, /it-eu/).\n5. Given a shopper is on any storefront other than EU Domestic, when they browse the site, then the language mismatch prompt is never triggered.\n\n*Cookie management for language mismatch:*\n\n# *Given* a shopper dismisses or acts on the language mismatch slide-out\n*When* the interaction is complete\n*Then* a required functional cookie is set in the shopper's browser suppressing the slide-out for X days\n# *Given* the cookie has been set\n*When* the shopper returns to the site within X days\n*Then* the language mismatch slide-out is not shown, regardless of browser-detected language mismatch\n# *Given* the cookie has expired (after X days)\n*When* the shopper returns to the site and their browser-detected language still does not match the storefront's language\n*Then* the language mismatch slide-out is shown again\n# *Given* the shopper clears their browser cookies\n*When* they return to the site and their browser-detected language does not match the storefront’s language\n*Then* the language mismatch slide-out is shown again, as no suppression cookie is present\n\nWe can start with 7 days but needs to be able to be changed."
  }
}"}

