content.content:
{"result":"{
  "id": "19104",
  "key": "SFCC-688",
  "summary": "Regional Storefronts — Country & Language Selector",
  "description": "As a Shopper, \nI want to be directed to the correct Zimmermann storefront for my location and be able to manually switch country, currency and language, \nso that I see local pricing, shipping options and content relevant to where I am.\n\n----\n\n**Image for reference (Figma is leading):** \n\n![\"image-20260826-035012.png\"](image-20260826-035012.png)\n\nThis story covers the experience of the country/language selector. The underlying PWA component (global/country-currency-selector) is built separately in the PWA Kit Components epic and consumed here. This story covers how they are triggered and behave from a shopper's perspective across storefronts.",
  "status": {
    "name": "Blocked",
    "category": "In Progress",
    "color": "yellow"
  },
  "labels": [
    "Custom",
    "REG-020",
    "REG-021",
    "REG-022",
    "REG-023",
    "REG-024",
    "REG-025",
    "REG-026",
    "REG-027",
    "Squad-A"
  ],
  "customfield_10231": {
    "value": "1. Given a shopper is on the AU storefront, when they browse the site, then the country selector is showing the country and currency but is not selectable and cross-storefront navigation is not available.\n2. Given a shopper is on any non-AU storefront, when they open the country selector from the footer, then countries are displayed grouped by region with their associated currency and a search field.\n3. Given a shopper opens the country selector, then they are warned that changing location may remove items from their bag before the redirect fires.\n4. Given a shopper selects a country that maps to the EU Domestic storefront, when they make that selection, then a language selector is presented showing English, Français, Italiano, and Español before the redirect fires.\n5. Given a shopper selects a language on the EU Domestic path, when they confirm, then they are redirected to the correct EU locale URL (e.g. /fr-eu/, /it-eu/, /es-eu/, /en-eu/).\n6. Given a shopper selects a country that maps to any storefront other than EU Domestic, when they confirm, then they are redirected directly to that storefront without a language selection step.\n7. Given a shopper selects China from the country selector, when they confirm, then they are routed to the HK storefront.\n8. Given a shopper selects Australia from the country selector on any non-AU storefront, when they confirm, then they are routed to the HK storefront."
  }
}"}

